# Separate Visibility & Animation — Specifications

## Animation-Control (New Capability)

## Purpose

A dedicated control for animation behavior that operates independently from bar visibility.

## Requirements

### Requirement: Animation Toggle Independence

The system SHALL support independent animation control that is separate from bar visibility.

#### Scenario: Toggle animation from MenuBarExtra

- GIVEN the app is running with animation enabled
- WHEN the user clicks "Start/Stop Animation" in MenuBarExtra
- THEN the animation SHALL start or stop immediately
- AND bar visibility SHALL remain unchanged

#### Scenario: Toggle animation from Settings

- GIVEN the user opens Settings → General
- WHEN the user toggles "Start/Stop Animation"
- THEN animation SHALL start or stop immediately
- AND bar visibility SHALL remain unchanged

#### Scenario: Default animation state

- GIVEN the app is launched
- THEN animation SHALL be disabled by default
- AND the bar SHALL be visible if visibility is enabled

#### Scenario: Animation on with bar hidden

- GIVEN the bar is hidden via visibility toggle
- WHEN the user enables animation
- THEN animation SHALL start
- AND the bar SHALL remain hidden

## Status-Bar (Modified Capability)

## Delta for status-bar

### MODIFIED Requirements

### Requirement: Status Bar Rendering

The system SHALL render a full-width colored bar at the top of the screen, below the system menu bar area.
(Previously: Rendering included animation control)

#### Scenario: Bar appears on launch

- GIVEN the app is launched
- THEN a bar SHALL be rendered across the full screen width
- AND the bar SHALL be 28pt tall, positioned at `screen.maxY - 28pt`

#### Scenario: Bar stays on all Spaces

- GIVEN the user switches Spaces or fullscreen apps
- THEN the bar SHALL remain visible on the current Space
- AND the bar SHALL NOT appear in the Mission Control / window switcher

#### Scenario: Visibility toggle still works (no regression)

- GIVEN the user enables or disables the feature via MenuBarExtra or Settings
- WHEN the toggle is used
- THEN the bar SHALL appear or disappear immediately
- AND animation SHALL remain unaffected by visibility changes